Inspect and Manage Defferred User Jobs
atq = used to list delayed user jobs queued up to run later via the at command.
-----------------------------------------
Remove Jobs from Schedule
atrm (JOBNUMBER)
----------------------------example using at-------------------------------
echo "date >> /home/student/myjob.txt" | at now +2min
atq = watch the queue
watch atq = to watch queue in real time
The command updates the output of the atq command every two seconds.
After the atd daemon removes the deferred job from the queue, press Ctrl+c to exit.
at -q g teatime
-q = is the queue flag
teatime = exactly at 16:00
at -q b 16:05
a = standard queue
b = batch jobs
A batch job is a task scheduled to run in the background only when the computer isn't busy.
By default, a batch job will only start when the system load average drops below 1.5.
c-z = have lower cpu priority
